      "id": "IS01",
      "type": "irony",
      "got_intended": true,
      "got_literal": false,
      "model_answer": "The speaker's statement, 'Well, this has been a delightful afternoon!' is an example of sarcasm. \n\nThe literal meaning of the sentence suggests that the speaker has had a pleasant and enjoyable experience. However, given the context that they have been waiting 2 hours in the rain for a bus, it's highly unlikely that they actually mean it.\n\nThe speaker's true intended meaning is the opposite of what they're saying. They're expressing frustration, annoyance, and possibly even disappointment or anger at having to wait for so long in uncomfortable conditions. The use of the word 'delightful' is ironic, and the tone is likely to be one of exasperation or irritation. \n\nIn essence, the speaker is being sarcastic, implying that the experience has been anything but delightful. They're using humor or irony to convey their dissatisfaction with the situation.",
      "marked_literal": false
    },
    {
      "id": "IS02",
      "type": "irony",
      "got_intended": true,
      "got_literal": false,
      "model_answer": "In this situation, the student says \"Another academic triumph!\" after receiving an F on a test. \n\nThe literal meaning of the phrase \"academic triumph\" is a great achievement or success in academic pursuits. However, given the context of receiving a failing grade, it's clear that the student is being sarcastic.\n\nThe speaker's TRUE intended meaning is the opposite of what they're literally saying. They're actually expressing disappointment, frustration, and possibly even irony or humor about their poor performance on the test. The student is using sarcasm to convey that receiving an F is not a triumph at all, but rather a failure. The tone is likely to be self-deprecating and humorous, rather than genuinely celebratory.",
      "marked_literal": false
